  "question": {
    "text": "The number of complex numbers $z$, satisfying $|z|=1$ and $\\left|\\frac{z}{\\bar{z}}+\\frac{\\bar{z}}{z}\\right|=1$, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "IaPCO",
      "text": "4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "K6zuW",
      "text": "8",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "QbrkM",
      "text": "10",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CyoJs",
      "text": "6",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& |z|=1 \\\\\n& \\left|\\frac{z}{\\bar{z}}+\\frac{\\bar{z}}{z}\\right|=1 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow\\left|z^2+(\\bar{z})^2\\right|=1\n\\end{aligned}$\nLet $z=x+i y$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow\\left|(x+i y)^2+(x-i y)^2\\right|=1 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow\\left|2 x^2-2 y^2\\right|=1 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow\\left|x^2-y^2\\right|=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow x^2-y^2=\\frac{ \\pm 1}{2} \\\\\n& \\text { and } x^2+y^2=1\n\\end{aligned}$\nCase I: $x^2-y^2=\\frac{1}{2}$\nCase II: $x^2-y^2=-\\frac{1}{2}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/og8TEMnqg76KtVOosOT0nmTKMc31yR69ZGORSa039Kg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
